# Sahaay Setu — Cursor rules

Frontend for SIH PS 26092 (MoSJE): a multilingual React Native app matching SC entrepreneurs
and students to concessional credit schemes and to Channel Partners who can process them.

## Read first, every session

1. `context/context.json` — what the project is, who owns what, where things live
2. `context/state.json` — current state, what's done, what's next
3. `.agents/PROTOCOL.md` — the working protocol shared with other AI tools

`context/decisions.json` records why things are the way they are. Read it before proposing a
change that contradicts one.

## Architecture

```
app/            expo-router routes (screens only, no business logic)
src/api/        contracts (Zod) · services · mock backend
src/features/   pure business logic (EMI math, rule engine)
src/components/ ui (generic) · domain (scheme/partner aware)
src/i18n/       6 locales, en.json is the baseline
src/theme/      design tokens — the only source of colour and spacing
```

Data flow is strictly `screen → hook → service → mock or HTTP`. A screen must never import
from `src/api/mock/` or call `fetch`.

## Conventions

- `@/` alias for `src` (Metro resolves it from tsconfig paths; there is no babel.config.js)
- All user-visible strings via `t()` into `src/i18n/locales/en.json`
- `Text` from `@/components/ui`, never react-native's — ours has Indic line heights
- Colours and spacing from `@/theme` only
- Touch targets ≥ 48dp, body text ≥ 16px, status never colour-only
- Money as whole-rupee integers, formatted via `@/utils/format`

## Skills

Read the matching playbook in `.agents/skills/` before starting that kind of work:
`sahaay-frontend` (screens/components) · `api-contract-change` (anything under `src/api/`) ·
`scheme-domain` (eligibility, EMI, partner routing) · `add-a-language` (i18n).

Each `SKILL.md` is short and points at `references/` files — one rule each, wrong example and
right example.

## Verify

```bash
npm run verify                        # typecheck + lint + i18n
npx expo export --platform android    # real bundle
```

## Data honesty

Scheme figures are unverified; all Channel Partner records are invented. They carry
`verified: false` and the UI shows warnings. Do not remove those warnings.

## Handoff

Update `context/state.json` when you finish something — set `updatedBy` to `cursor`, add
`verified` entries with the command output that proves them, and adjust `next`. Claude Code
reads the same file.
